@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Health endpoint is public - should return 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### 2. Asset endpoint without token - should return 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/assets


### 3. Register a normal user - should return 201 Created with a token
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Day 9 User",
  "email": "day09.user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}


### 4. Login normal user - should return 200 OK with a token
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day09.user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}


### 5. Asset endpoint with USER token - should return 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.$.token}}


### 6. Create asset with USER token - should return 403 Forbidden
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginUser.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "DAY9-USER-0001",
  "name": "User Test Asset",
  "category": "Test",
  "serialNumber": "SN-DAY9-USER-0001",
  "location": "Training Room"
}


### 7. Login seeded admin - should return 200 OK with a token
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}


### 8. Create asset with ADMIN token - should return 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/assets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assetTag": "DAY9-ADMIN-0001",
  "name": "Admin Test Asset",
  "category": "Test",
  "serialNumber": "SN-DAY9-ADMIN-0001",
  "location": "Training Room"
}
